\code{d(f, x)} differentiates \code{f} with respect to the variable \code{x};
\code{d(f, x, x)} gives the second derivative and \code{d(f, x, t)} a mixed
derivative. The function returns the expression that should equal
zero, or a list of such expressions for a system of equations. For
the viscous Burgers equation \eqn{u_t + u u_x - \nu u_{xx} = 0}:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{function(u, x, t, nu, d) d(u, t) + u * d(u, x) - nu * d(u, x, x)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

